<div xmlns:perseus="http://www.perseus.org/meta/perseus.rdfs#" xmlns:dctype="http://purl.org/dc/dcmitype/" xmlns:tufts="http://www.tufts.edu/" xmlns:alph="http://alpheios.net/namespaces/tei" class="alpheios-lex-text_container en">
    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n64903" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">μάνδρα</span></b> , ἡ, <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>A.</b><i>enclosed space</i>,
			</div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense3"><b>1.</b> for cattle, <i>fold,
				byre</i>, <i><span class="en">
				Call.
				<u>Cer.</u>
				106
			</span></i>, <i><span class="en">
				Theoc.
				4.61
			</span></i>, <i><span class="en">
				Plu.
				2.648a
			</span></i>; for horses, 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">μάνδραις ἐν ἱππείαισιν</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					S.
					<u>Fr.</u>
					659.3
				</span></i>
			: in reference to the bezel in which the stone of a ring, with
			a design of oxen, is set, <i><span class="en">
				Pl.
				<u>Epigr.</u>
				21
			</span></i>, <i><span class="en">
				<u>AP</u>
				9.746
			</span></i> (<span class="entity">Polemo</span>), cf. <i><span class="en">
				Hld.
				5.14
			</span></i>. </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense3"><b>2.</b> dub. sens. in
				<i><span class="en">
				<u>POxy.</u>
				984
			</span></i>
			<span class="entity">(i A. D.)</span>. </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense3"><b>3.</b>
			<i>square</i> on a draught-board, <i><span class="en">
				Mart.
				7.72.8
			</span></i> (pl.).</div>
    </div> <div class="alpheios-lex-footnotes en"> </div>
